    {
      "repository": "NVIDIA/SkillEvaluator",
      "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillEvaluator",
      "trending_rank": 12,
      "description": "A test bench for AI agent skills from NVIDIA: it checks a skill folder for safety and format, flags duplicated guidance, then runs an agent with and without the skill in a sandbox to measure whether it helps.",
      "why_interesting": "Skill libraries are multiplying fast, and this asks the useful question: ==does the skill actually change the result?== Its Skill Lift score compares runs against a no-skill baseline, and version 0.9.0 adds spending budgets, version comparisons and reports that show which expectations were met or left unchecked.",
      "caveat": "NVIDIA labels it ==experimental, with community best-effort support and no SLA==. Static checks run without a model, but full checks fetch extra security scanners, and live evaluation needs a model provider, a supported agent and Docker; model and sandbox use can cost money.",
      "category": "AI agents / evaluation",
      "language": "Python",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
