      "repository": "elementalsouls/Claude-BugHunter",
      "url": "https://github.com/elementalsouls/Claude-BugHunter",
      "trending_rank": 9,
      "description": "A skill bundle for authorized bug hunting and external red-team work: 83 skills and 15 slash commands for Claude Code, also loadable by other agents, covering recon, web vulnerability classes, enterprise platform attack chains, validation and report writing.",
      "why_interesting": "Instead of one generic security prompt, it splits the work into ==per-class skills built from 681 disclosed HackerOne reports==, with a scope and validation gate before anything is submitted. The README is explicit about what it leaves out, such as internal Active Directory attacks, C2 and evasion.",
      "caveat": "This is ==offensive tooling, for assets you own or are authorized to test==. It is a single maintainer's project with commercial sponsors, its 'battle-tested' claims are unverified, and the copy installer writes into the skill folders of several agents and can wire in a Burp MCP server.",
