      "description": "Agent skills for Google Stitch, an AI design tool: they let a coding agent generate and edit screens, extract a DESIGN.md from existing code, and turn Stitch designs into React, React Native or shadcn/ui components.",
      "why_interesting": "It joins design and code in one agent loop: ==code goes up into Stitch as designs, and designs come back as components==. The skills follow the open Agent Skills format, so the same folders work in Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI and, with manual setup, OpenCode.",
      "caveat": "Every skill ==needs the Stitch MCP server and a Stitch account==, so design data goes to Google's service. The README says it is not an officially supported Google product, and the repository's last push was on 17 August.",
